+
+  case('SYMLIST')
+! every crystal symmetry: its 3x3 integer lattice rotation (the spatial part,
+! via lsplsymc), its fractional translation, and whether that translation is
+! zero -- enough for the Python side to identify a C_n rotation and its axis
+! without duplicating Elk's space-group analysis
+    write(*,*) nsymcrys,nspinor
